---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---
<Layout
  title="Hanfu Accessories: The Complete Guide"
  description="Every Hanfu accessory explained: hairpins and buyao, fans, belts and sashes, shoes, sachets, jade, and the accessory system for each dynasty."
  canonicalUrl="https://www.dresses-hanfu.com/guides/accessories/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Guides", url: "/guides" }, { name: "Hanfu Accessories", url: "/guides/accessories" }]}
  articleSchema={{
    datePublished: "2026-08-01",
    dateModified: "2026-08-08",
    author: { "@type": "Person", "name": "Hanfu Dress Guide Editorial Team" }
  }}
>
  <SiteHeader active="/guides/how-to-wear" />
  <main>
    <article>
      <section class="section" style="padding-bottom: 2rem;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <p style="font-size:0.8125rem;color:var(--color-muted);margin-bottom:1rem;"><a href="/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/guides/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">Guides</a> &rsaquo; Hanfu Accessories</p>
          <h1>Hanfu Accessories: The Complete Accessory System</h1>
          <p class="lead" style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:1.5rem;line-height:1.55;">
            Accessories are where a Hanfu look becomes personal. Traditionally, they also signaled rank, season, and occasion. Here's the full system — from hairpins to jade — and where to learn more about each piece.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <h2>The Full Accessory Glossary</h2>

          <div class="vs-card" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size:1rem;">Hairpins (Zan) &amp; Buyao</h3>
            <p>The foundation of Hanfu hair. Single pins, two-prong chai, and the dangling buyao ("step-shake") anchor the hairstyle and mark age and status. <a href="/accessories/hairpins/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">Full hairpin guide →</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="vs-card" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size:1rem;">Fan (Shan)</h3>
            <p>The folding fan and round tuanshan. In summer a practical item, in court a social language — how you held the fan said something. Artists and scholars of the Song favored the folding fan. <a href="/accessories/fans/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">Full fan guide →</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="vs-card" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size:1rem;">Shoes (Lu / Xue)</h3>
            <p>Embroidered cloth shoes (xie) with flat soles or cloud-head toes, varying by gender and occasion. Brides wear red embroidered shoes; scholars favor simple flat styles. <a href="/accessories/shoes/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">Full shoe guide →</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="vs-card" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size:1rem;">Belts &amp; Sashes (Yao dai)</h3>
            <p>The functional fastening and a display item. Some belt ends are ornamented with jade, gold rings or more. In every dynasty, the belt marked rank from the common belt of leather to imperial clasped belts. <a href="/accessories/belts/" style="color:var(--color-accent);">Full belt guide →</a></p>
          </div>
          <div class="vs-card" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size:1rem;">Sachets &amp; Beaded Pendants</h3>
            <p>Fragrant sachets (xiangbao) hung at the waist scented the space round the wearer. Jade pebi and other pendants (pei) were worn at the belt, their symbolism layered with auspicious motifs.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="vs-card" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">
            <h3 style="font-size:1rem;">Jade and Metal Jewels</h3>
            <p>Jade collars, earrings, hat ivory, and belt buckles. Jade was the gentleman's stone — worn by men for virtue, by women for beauty. Beyond jade: gold, silver, and wood varied by dynasty and budget.</p>
          </div>

          <h2 style="margin-top:3rem;">Accessories by Dynasty</h2>
          <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
            <table class="size-ref-table" style="margin-top:1rem;">
              <thead><tr><th>Dynasty</th><th>Key Accessories</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><strong>Han</strong></td><td>Jade pendants, simple hairpins, belt plaques</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Tang</strong></td><td>Hairpin sets, gold ornaments, necklaces, fans, perfume sachets (cosmopolitan exchange)</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Song</strong></td><td>Subdued jade, silver hairpins, scholar's fans</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Ming</strong></td><td>Ornamentation peaked — gold filigree, pearls, the phoenix crown, complex belts</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <div style="margin-top:3rem;padding:2rem;background:var(--color-accent-light);border-radius:var(--radius-md);">
            <p style="font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;font-family:var(--font-display);">Dive Into Each Accessory</p>
            <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.75rem;margin-top:1rem;">
              <a href="/accessories/hairpins/" class="btn btn-outline">Hairpins</a>
              <a href="/accessories/fans/" class="btn btn-outline">Fans</a>
              <a href="/accessories/shoes/" class="btn btn-outline">Shoes</a>
              <a href="/accessories/belts/" class="btn btn-outline">Belts &amp; Sashes</a>
              <a href="/guides/how-to-wear/" class="btn btn-outline">How to Wear</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>